# Static-asset headers (Workers assets / Pages convention).
# Baseline security headers for every path ([AU] AMENDMENTS-AUDIT-2026-11 AU-5,
# audit SEC-3). No Cache-Control here: this rule also reaches a missing /_next/ file
# (see the last comment of this file). Rules that match the same path are merged, and
# a header two of them set is sent as "a, b": a later rule that needs another value
# for one of these five must detach it first ("! Name"), as the grown-up block that
# scripts/app-host/merge-console.mjs appends does. A script-source policy is not here:
# it needs a report-only period first.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self'
# The app's own script chunks: content-hashed names, so a file never changes at its URL and
# is cached for a year (AMENDMENTS-FINISH-2026-11 FN-3). A chunk the host does not have is
# answered 404 by the app host's Worker (scripts/app-host/worker.mjs), never with index.html,
# so no page can be kept under a chunk URL; this rule is the only Cache-Control of these
# paths. They also stay the one exception to nosniff (F-CURR-002 section 10,
# pwa/lesson-chunks.mjs nosniffLessonChunks, which fails the build otherwise): should a chunk
# URL of an older build ever get the fallback page again (a host without the Worker), the
# browser runs it and the page reloads onto the new build. The other four headers stay.
/_expo/static/js/*
  ! X-Content-Type-Options
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
# The service worker and manifest must never be served stale, or an update
# could take up to a day to reach installed apps.
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/manifest.webmanifest
  Content-Type: application/manifest+json
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
# Recorded clips (F-AUDIO-004 §3.10): Expo mirrors assets/audio/** under
# /assets/assets/audio/ with a content hash in every file name, so a clip
# never changes at its URL. The one rule covers every group, the text-keyed
# /assets/assets/audio/say/ clips included (AMENDMENTS-AUDIO-CLIPS AC-B6,
# runtime cache hr-audio-say-v1): a second, narrower rule would join its
# Cache-Control to this one, so there is none.
/assets/assets/audio/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
# Grown-up console chunks (F-APP-001 §3.3, A-3): /_next/ gets no year-long rule here.
# Unlike apps/web (404-page), this Worker's single-page fallback answers a missing chunk
# with index.html, and an immutable rule would let a browser keep that page under the
# chunk URL for a year; the Worker stays assets-only (AD-1), so the rule is dropped and
# chunks revalidate. scripts/app-host/merge-console.mjs refuses a build that adds it back,
# and appends the grown-up page rules (§3.17) to the dist copy of this file.
